# System Flow Diagrams

## 1. Auth: Register -> Verify OTP -> Login -> Token Exchange

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant Auth as Auth Provider
    participant Redis as Redis
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    User->>FE: Submit register form
    FE->>Auth: POST /auth/register
    Auth->>DB: Create user(active=false)
    Auth->>DB: Create user_role=STUDENT
    Auth->>Redis: Store OTP payload (TTL)
    Auth-->>FE: verify_code + message
    FE-->>User: Show OTP screen

    User->>FE: Submit OTP
    FE->>Auth: GET /auth/verify?otp=...
    Auth->>Redis: Read OTP payload
    Auth->>DB: Mark user.active=true
    Auth-->>FE: Verified account successfully
    FE-->>User: Redirect to login

    User->>FE: Submit login form
    FE->>Auth: POST /auth/login (form data)
    Auth->>DB: Validate user + roles
    Auth->>Redis: Create authorization_code
    Auth-->>FE: code + redirect_uri

    FE->>Auth: POST /auth/code
    Auth->>DB: Load user roles
    Auth-->>FE: access_token + refresh_token
    FE-->>User: Store auth state / cookies

    alt invalid otp or expired code
        Auth-->>FE: 404/400 error
        FE-->>User: Show resend or retry state
    else wrong password
        Auth-->>FE: 401 Unauthorized
        FE-->>User: Show login error
    end

## 2. Course Catalog -> Course Detail -> Enrollment / Purchase

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Student
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant API as Business App API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant PayOS as PayOS

    Student->>FE: Open course catalog
    FE->>API: GET /api/v1/courses?page=&size=&q=&price_type=
    API->>DB: Query published courses
    API-->>FE: Paginated course list
    FE-->>Student: Render catalog cards + filters

    Student->>FE: Open course detail
    FE->>API: GET /api/v1/courses/{slug}
    API->>DB: Load course + sections + lessons
    API-->>FE: Course detail payload
    FE-->>Student: Render curriculum and CTA

    alt free course
        Student->>FE: Click enroll
        FE->>API: POST /api/v1/courses/{slug}/enroll
        API->>DB: Create enrollment
        API-->>FE: ENROLLED
        FE-->>Student: Show "Vào học ngay"
    else paid course
        Student->>FE: Click buy
        FE->>API: POST /api/v1/payments/payos/create
        API->>DB: Create transaction=PENDING
        API->>PayOS: Create checkout link
        PayOS-->>API: payos_link + qrcode
        API-->>FE: payment payload
        FE-->>Student: Show checkout page
    end

    alt payment webhook success
        PayOS->>API: POST webhook
        API->>DB: Update transaction=COMPLETE
        API->>DB: Unlock enrollment/ownership
        API-->>FE: success event
        FE-->>Student: Redirect to classroom
    else payment failed or expired
        API-->>FE: failed/expired status
        FE-->>Student: Show retry state
    end

## 3. Classroom: Lesson Content + Comment Thread + Progress

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Student
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant API as Business App API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Student->>FE: Open classroom lesson
    FE->>API: GET /api/v1/student/courses/{slug}/study
    API->>DB: Load sections, lessons, lesson contents, progress
    API-->>FE: Curriculum + current content state
    FE-->>Student: Render sidebar + main content

    Student->>FE: Open lesson comments
    FE->>API: GET /api/v1/lesson-contents/{id}/comments
    API->>DB: Load top-level comments + replies
    API-->>FE: Comment tree
    FE-->>Student: Render thread

    Student->>FE: Post comment
    FE->>API: POST /api/v1/lesson-contents/{id}/comment
    API->>DB: Validate lesson content and parent_id
    API->>DB: Insert comment
    API-->>FE: Created comment
    FE-->>Student: Append to thread

    alt reading complete
        Student->>FE: Click complete
        FE->>API: POST /api/v1/student/progress/lesson-content/{id}/complete
        API->>DB: Upsert lesson_content_progress
        API-->>FE: completion state
        FE-->>Student: Mark as completed
    else comment invalid or unauthorized
        API-->>FE: 401/403/404 error
        FE-->>Student: Show validation/error state
    end

## 4. Teacher Register -> Admin Review -> Role Promotion

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor TeacherCandidate as Student/Teacher Candidate
    actor Admin
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant API as Business App API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Redis as Redis

    TeacherCandidate->>FE: Submit teacher registration form
    FE->>API: POST /api/v1/teacher-register
    API->>DB: Validate duplicate pending/approved request
    API->>DB: Insert teacher_register=PENDING
    API->>Redis: Queue verification notification/job
    API-->>FE: pending response
    FE-->>TeacherCandidate: Show submitted state

    Admin->>FE: Open review dashboard
    FE->>API: GET /api/v1/admin/teacher-registers
    API->>DB: Load pending applications
    API-->>FE: Review list
    FE-->>Admin: Render compare panel

    Admin->>FE: Approve / reject request
    FE->>API: PUT /api/v1/admin/teacher-registers/{id}
    API->>DB: Update register status
    alt approve
        API->>DB: Insert TEACHER role
        API->>DB: Create/activate teacher_profile
        API-->>FE: approved response
        FE-->>Admin: Show success toast
    else reject
        API->>DB: Store reviewed_note
        API-->>FE: rejected response
        FE-->>Admin: Show rejected state
    end

## 5. Problem Submit + Judge Result

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Student
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant API as Business App API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Judge as Judge Service

    Student->>FE: Submit code
    FE->>API: POST /api/v1/problems/{slug}/submit
    API->>DB: Create submission=PENDING
    API->>Judge: Dispatch job with code, language, testcases
    Judge->>Judge: Compile/run inside sandbox
    Judge-->>API: Result (AC/WA/TLE/MLE/CE/RE)
    API->>DB: Update submission status, score, runtime, memory
    alt accepted
        API->>DB: Mark lesson progress complete if needed
        API-->>FE: accepted result
        FE-->>Student: Show AC + progress update
    else failure
        API-->>FE: failure result
        FE-->>Student: Show stderr/stdout diff / error panel
    end

## 6. AI Interview Session

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Student
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant API as Business App API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Student->>FE: Start interview
    FE->>API: POST /api/v1/interviews/sessions
    API->>DB: Create interview_session
    API-->>FE: session_id + first_question
    FE-->>Student: Render chat UI

    loop chat turns
        Student->>FE: Send answer
        FE->>API: POST /api/v1/interviews/sessions/{sessionId}/chat
        API->>DB: Persist interview_message
        API-->>FE: next AI question / stream event
        FE-->>Student: Append chat bubble + loading state
    end

    Student->>FE: Finish session
    FE->>API: GET /api/v1/interviews/sessions/{sessionId}/report
    API->>DB: Load transcript and report
    API-->>FE: report payload
    FE-->>Student: Render score + strengths + weaknesses

